#!/bin/zsh
TMUX=/opt/homebrew/bin/tmux
[ -x "$TMUX" ] || TMUX=/usr/local/bin/tmux
send() { $TMUX send-keys -t $1 C-u; sleep 1; $TMUX send-keys -t $1 "$2"; sleep 2; $TMUX send-keys -t $1 Enter; sleep 2; $TMUX send-keys -t $1 Enter; sleep 1; echo "sent -> $1"; }

send split-speaker:1.1 "GO - serve it on 8796. 18.5 minutes against my 15 is fine; you were right to hold the length rather than shorten clips, because clip length is the variable that actually moved the can't-tell rate. Two things I want on record. FIRST, the two serve.py bugs you caught are the more valuable half of this build: ID_RE would have 400'd every single answer, and audio_ids looked for clips/p....wav so ready would never have gone true and the page would have sat on still-being-prepared forever. Neither is visible by reading the page. You found both by asserting the invariant against a synthetic manifest before touching the real one - the same habit that caught the chunk-offset defect. That is now three real defects from one practice; keep it. SECOND, your push-back is noted and correct: one doctor has ZERO clips clearing the strict rule, so for him material quality is still live and v6 cannot answer it. Do not let that get lost when the results come in - report him separately rather than folding him into an average. When V finishes, score it with the identity pairs first as the attention floor, then same and different as the discrimination measure, then the OPEN pairs, which are the ones I actually want: same slot, different diarizer speaker index. If V says same person on those, the diarizer is OVER-splitting - one doctor scattered across several identities - which is the mirror of the gluing and it governs how clips get pooled."

send scribe:1.1 "V has answered the transcript_enabled question: the 211 rooms are OFF deliberately, BUT his words are - eventually i do want to transcribe all of it. So design for that, do not act on it. Concretely: the join-only path should NOT touch transcript-disabled rooms by default, but it must be able to target them with one explicit parameter rather than a rebuild, so that when V says go it is a flag and not a fortnight. Making a clip is only joining audio, not transcribing it, so the flag's intent is not violated by having the clip ready - but I am not going to pre-build clips for rooms someone deliberately switched off without him asking. Keep the two decisions separate in the code and say so in the handoff. Everything else in the order stands."
